[
 {
  "name": "usage",
  "args": [
   "hl"
  ],
  "exit": 2,
  "stdout": "usage.out.txt",
  "stderr": [
   "Usage: hl <dump.hprof | profile.json> [top]",
   "       hl peaks <dump.hprof | profile.json> [top]",
   "       hl leaks <dump.hprof | profile.json> [top] [--share <percent>]",
   "       hl diff <before> <after> [top] [--share <percent>]",
   "       hl <dump.hprof | profile.json> --trace <class>",
   "       hl <dump.hprof> --save <profile.json>",
   "       hl <dump.hprof> --stats",
   "       hl <dump.hprof> --oops compressed|wide",
   "Both input kinds are read: a .hprof is parsed, a profile.json saved from an",
   "earlier run is read as it is, so several reports can share one parse.",
   "The parse of a dump is kept next to it, as <name>.hl.json, and read back by",
   "the next command on the same dump: --fresh parses again, --no-keep keeps none.",
   "--json prints one JSON document instead of text. Exit codes: 0 found, 1 broke,",
   "2 called wrong, 3 found nothing, 4 a traced name matches several classes."
  ]
 },
